<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">José de la Serna</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1770–1832</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">José de la Serna was a Spanish general and the last <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroy-of-india">viceroy</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a>, from 1821 to 1824. Royalist officers made him viceroy by deposing Joaquín de la Pezuela in January 1821; he abandoned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lima">Lima</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jose-de-san-martin">José de San Martín</a> later that year and continued the war from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cusco">Cusco</a>. Wounded and captured at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-ayacucho">Battle of Ayacucho</a> on 9 December 1824, he saw the capitulation that ended Spanish rule in Peru.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jose-de-la-serna.jpg" alt="José de la Serna" width="320" height="459" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Retrato_del_conde_de_los_Andes.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
